  {
    "id": "4aee3809-bf8b-5b44-88e5-66446f308455",
    "pack": "knights-of-lastwall",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:campaign-stable",
    "name": "Campaign Stable",
    "level": 8,
    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "traits": ["magical", "structure"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "knights-of-lastwall"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Used to facilitate the care of mounts during long campaigns or when it's necessary to move camp frequently, this object appears to be a simple, worn wooden horseshoe."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Activate",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (1 minute) command, Interact"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Frequency",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " once per day"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Effect",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You place the horseshoe on the ground and it unfolds into a spacious stable with a wide central aisle, stalls to accommodate up to eight horses, and sufficient feed and water to sustain the horses for 1 day. The stalls can house other quadrupedal mounts, but the stable provides only horse feed, which might be unsuitable for other creatures. As a 1-minute activity, which has the concentrate trait, you can alter the shape of the stalls to accommodate different mounts, though the space available within the stable never changes, only the layout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A metal horseshoe hangs inside the stable near the entrance. You can remove the horseshoe with an Interact action, which causes the stable to fold into the horseshoe, leaving it again looking as if it's made of worn wood."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.XZleXDXQ5eThTLWd"
    },
    "data": {
      "price": {
        "coins": {
          "gp": 500
        }
      },
      "bulk": "light",
      "activations": [
        {
          "slug": "campaign-stable",
          "name": "Campaign Stable",
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "day"
          }
        }
      ],
      "usage": {
        "type": "held",
        "hands": "one"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "e63ad381-fbbb-54ac-8f4c-cfef3f82088b",
    "pack": "knights-of-lastwall",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:detector-stone",
    "name": "Detector Stone",
    "level": 7,
    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "traits": ["invested", "magical"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "knights-of-lastwall"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "During their journeys across the Gravelands, the Knights of Lastwall found several smoky, gemstone-like objects that knights refer to as "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "detector stones",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Some of the knights' Magaambyan allies believe the stones are "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "aeon stones",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " corrupted by the same energies that corrupted the Gravelands, though they don't display the characteristic orbiting behavior of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "aeon stones",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " when invested. Despite the controversy, many knights use the stones for their ability to detect the presence of undead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "While you have a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "detector stone",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " invested, it glows faintly when an undead creature is within 30 feet of you, unless the undead is "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "d851e3ca-be0d-55a7-a4d1-d7ed8b7ecafa"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or disguised with a Deception or Stealth result of 20 or higher. An invested stone may be carried in a pocket, but some knights set them in necklaces, bracelets, or weapon hilts."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Activate",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "action-cost",
            "cost": "one"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " envision"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Frequency",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " once per minute"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Effect",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You channel your life-force into the stone, empowering it temporarily. The stone can detect undead within 60 feet of you, rather than 30 feet, until the end of your turn. Undead hiding or disguising themselves must make an additional Deception or Stealth check to remain disguised or hidden from the activation, and the DC of the check is 23 rather than 20."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Activate",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "action-cost",
            "cost": "two"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " envision, Interact"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Frequency",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " once per hour"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Effect",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You focus on the stone as it glows, and your eyes glow with the same tainted light. You detect the auras of evil undead in a 30-foot radius around you and learn each aura's location and strength. This has the effects of a 2nd-rank "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "detect alignment",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " spell but only detects evil undead."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.znWf2DgWyElwzQwJ"
    },
    "data": {
      "price": {
        "coins": {
          "gp": 360
        }
      },
      "bulk": "negligible",
      "activations": [
        {
          "slug": "detector-stone",
          "name": "Detector Stone",
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "minute"
          }
        }
      ],
      "usage": {
        "type": "worn"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "9d33edd0-9ba4-5eb1-8dca-463244da4d41",
    "pack": "knights-of-lastwall",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:hollowed-hilt",
    "name": "Hollowed Hilt",
    "level": 0,
    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "knights-of-lastwall"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A hollowed hilt is a weapon modification that allows a pommel to be detached and its hilt meticulously hollowed out to create a small compartment without greatly affecting its balance. Often used by knight emissaries to hide important missives, this space can hold an object of light Bulk about the size of a scroll. A creature studying the weapon can find the hilt compartment with a successful "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "perception",
            "dc": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check. Any weapon with an appropriate hilt or pommel can be converted into a hollowed one by paying the equipment's price."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.ETwv7GshGM9IXnqH"
    },
